              "value": "Certificate and key from the 'tls' section of sepp.yaml; client certificate verification is off unless 'verify_client' is set"
            },
            {
              "name": "pkic:profile:integrationConstraints",
              "value": "The server context (lib/sbi/nghttp2-server.c) allows TLS 1.0 to 1.3 and sets the group list to P-256 only, so the server negotiates ECDHE on P-256 whatever the client offers. OpenSSL 3 refuses TLS 1.0 and 1.1 at its default security level. TLS 1.2 suites are ECDHE-ECDSA and ECDHE-RSA with AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305, and DHE-RSA with AES-GCM; TLS 1.3 suites are the OpenSSL defaults, with server preference. The client side (lib/sbi/client.c) uses libcurl with OpenSSL and its default groups. There is no setting for the group list. The SEPP advertises TLS as its only N32-f security capability. Library version from an Ubuntu 24.04 build; to confirm."
            },
            {
